    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, im looking at some paperwork for a house in seattle and im kind of lost. what actually is \"escrow\" and why do they need my money held by someone else instead of just giving it to the seller?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hi! Escrow is an arrangement where a neutral third party holds and regulates the payment of the funds required for two parties involved in a given transaction, such as a property purchase. The purpose of escrow is to ensure that both the buyer and seller meet their obligations before the transfer of ownership and the funds. It also protects both parties from a bad deal and provides peace of mind that the money will be used specifically for agreed-upon terms, like paying off the seller or covering various costs associated with the transaction.",
