      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel uncertain. Escrow companies are responsible and regulated entities, similar to banks, and they use established legal and financial systems to ensure everything is handled properly. They can't just disappear with your money, as they are bound by law, industry standards, and necessary qualifications to serve as an escrow agent. This ensures that your money will be used as intended and provides a level of security in the transaction. However, always verify the legitimacy of the company and check if they're registered with a reliable regulatory body. Additionally, it's wise to follow up with your real estate agent or attorney to ensure all the proper checks and balances are in place.",
