    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, so it's basically just a layer of trust. i guess i'm just nervous because it's such a large amount of money just sitting in a middleman's account waiting for everything to clear. is there any specific way the escrow agent tracks all that 'held' money so it doesn't get mixed up with their own stuff?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The escrow agent tracks the funds with meticulous record-keeping, separating your money from their own financial resources. They account for payments in separate transaction ledgers and follow up on the settlement of documents. Usually, there's a clear chain of custody of the funds, and the escrow agent issues receipts and transfers advice, ensuring that funds move only when both the buyer and seller have met their contractual obligations. Moreover, all financial statements and operations of escrow companies are subject to audits and must comply with strict financial regulations, so mixing up funds with their own is against law and very uncommon.",
